✅ Step 1 – Start Jenkins in Docker
🔹 Create volume
docker volume create jenkins-data
🔹 Run Jenkins (Windows → single line)
docker run -d --name jenkins -p 8080:8080 -p 50000:50000 -v jenkins-data:/var/jenkins_home -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock jenkins/jenkins:lts
✅ Step 2 – Get Admin Password
docker exec jenkins cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword

👉 Copy password
👉 Open browser:

http://localhost:8080
Paste password
Click Install suggested plugins
✅ Step 3 – Install Required Plugin

Go to:

Manage Jenkins → Manage Plugins

Install:

Docker Pipeline Plugin
✅ Step 4 – Install Docker inside Jenkins
docker exec -u root jenkins bash -c "apt-get update && apt-get install -y docker.io"

👉 Fix permission (important):

docker exec -u root jenkins chmod 666 /var/run/docker.sock
